# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Smartious Homeschool — Netlify _redirects
# Place this file in the build output (frontend/public/_redirects)
# so Netlify serves it at the site root.
#
# Rules are processed top-to-bottom; first match wins.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── FORCE STRIP TRAILING SLASHES (SEO canonicalization) ─────────
# Google Search Console reported /foo showing as 'Page with redirect'
# and /foo/ showing as 'Alternative page with proper canonical tag'.
# Root cause: Netlify was normalizing trailing slashes automatically
# while our canonical tag stripped them, creating a conflict.
# Combined with the prerender.js change (flat .html files instead of
# folder/index.html), this ensures ONE canonical URL per page.
# The '!' (force flag) makes this rule fire even when a file exists.
/*/                      /:splat                     301!

# ─── Country hub canonical consolidation (301s) ──────────────────
/us-families             /online-school/usa          301
/ca-families             /online-school/canada       301
/homeschooling-kenya     /online-school/kenya        301

# ─── SPA fallback — MUST be last so it doesn't override above ────
/*                       /index.html                 200
